{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Send one of you.</b> And afterward he reversed course and sent all of them except one, for Joseph wanted them to feel the sin they had committed against their brother and to confess their iniquity. And when they would send one of them, he thought that surely Reuben, the eldest of the brothers, would go, for upon him falls the prerogative of the firstborn to go out to freedom from the place of confinement. And perhaps the brothers would conclude that since Reuben had had no part in the selling, therefore he was spared — for even Judah had a part in this, for on this account the brothers deposed him from his greatness, as Rashi explained on the verse ״וַיֵּרֶד יְהוּדָה״ (Genesis 38:1). And after they had been in confinement three days, Joseph thought that this iniquity had already been purged; therefore he sent all of them except Simeon, for he had had the greatest part in his sale more than any of them. For what is stated ״וַיֹּאמְרוּ אִישׁ אֶל אָחִיו לְכוּ וְנַהַרְגֵהוּ״ (Genesis 37:20) — it was Simeon who said thus to Levi, as Rashi explained on the verse ״שִׁמְעוֹן וְלֵוִי אַחִים״ (Genesis 49:5). And surely Simeon began to speak thus, for Levi would not have spoken in the presence of one greater than himself. And so Rashi explained here. And all this he did so that they would recognize their sin and confess."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:10.703412403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}